<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kingdom of Great Britain</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Great Britain</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kingdom of Great <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> was the state created by the union of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> in 1707. It united the two realms under one parliament at Westminster and combined their commercial and colonial interests. Its growing naval and financial power provided the foundation for the expansion of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a> in the eighteenth century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-great-britain.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Great Britain" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hoshie · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Great_Britain_(1707%E2%80%931800).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
